{"unit_id": "pair_20058_197209", "ok": true, "issues": [], "snap_stats": {"exact": 26, "ws_normalized": 0, "no_match": 0, "anchor_only": 0, "empty": 0}, "parsed": {"unit_id": "pair_20058_197209", "passages": [{"passage_text": "The Fed came close to sounding a retreat in September, according to an official account of its meeting published Wednesday. Officials were united that the bond-buying campaign begun last year had produced the desired improvement in job growth. Most officials also agreed that the Fed should start pulling back by the end of 2013. But during an unusually fractious meeting, some officials worried that the gains might not be sustainable and argued that it was \"prudent\" to postpone retreat, according to the account.", "passage_polarity": "neutral", "signals": [{"signal_text": "according to an official account of its meeting published Wednesday", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "neutral", "rubric_matches": [2, 3], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "during an unusually fractious meeting", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "neutral", "rubric_matches": [66, 50], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "some officials worried that the gains might not be sustainable", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "neutral", "rubric_matches": [8, 30], "_snap_kind": "exact"}], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"passage_text": "A number of officials, \"pointed to heightened uncertainty about the course of federal fiscal policy over coming months, including the potential for a government shutdown or strains related to the debt ceiling debate,\" the account said. Any differences were papered over in a 9-to-1 vote to keep adding $85 billion a month to the Fed's holdings of Treasury securities and mortgage-backed securities, with the goal of reducing borrowing costs for businesses and consumers.", "passage_polarity": "neutral", "signals": [{"signal_text": "pointed to heightened uncertainty about the course of federal fiscal policy", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "neutral", "rubric_matches": [7, 30], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "Any differences were papered over in a 9-to-1 vote", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "neutral", "rubric_matches": [12, 34], "_snap_kind": "exact"}], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"passage_text": "Three weeks later, it seems even less likely that the Fed is on the verge of retreat. The government has shut down partly, depriving the Fed of fresh economic data, among other consequences, and the fight over the debt ceiling is intensifying. The Fed's leadership also is in transition. President Obama announced the nomination Wednesday of Janet L. Yellen, the Fed's vice chairwoman and a leading proponent of the stimulus, to succeed Ben S. Bernanke, the chairman, when he departs in January.", "passage_polarity": "negative", "signals": [{"signal_text": "The government has shut down partly, depriving the Fed of fresh economic data", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [9, 13], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "The Fed's leadership also is in transition", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "neutral", "rubric_matches": [66, 50], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "President Obama announced the nomination Wednesday of Janet L. Yellen", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "neutral", "rubric_matches": [2, 19], "_snap_kind": "exact"}], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"passage_text": "Ms. Yellen on Wednesday made clear her commitment to the stimulus campaign. \"Too many Americans still can't find a job, and worry how they'll pay their bills,\" she said. \"The Federal Reserve can help.\" Image Vincent R. Reinhart, chief United States economist at Morgan Stanley, wrote that the outcome of the September meeting already reflected Ms. Yellen's growing influence and focus on reducing unemployment, as well as Mr. Bernanke's impending departure. \"Bernanke had already left the building,\" he wrote, \"in spirit if not in body.\"",