{"unit_id": "pair_19140_50990", "ok": false, "issues": ["passage[2].signal[0] could not snap to passage (kind=anchor_only)"], "snap_stats": {"exact": 30, "ws_normalized": 0, "no_match": 0, "anchor_only": 1, "empty": 0}, "parsed": {"unit_id": "pair_19140_50990", "passages": [{"passage_text": "The push, which will include LEGO tie-in sets, Random House books, and (most refreshingly) Mattel action figures, is the full Monty in terms of Warner Bros. and DC Comics making a genuine effort to sell their superhero properties to audiences beyond the stereotypical young boy demographic. It is something that on its face is a net-positive.", "passage_polarity": "positive", "signals": [{"signal_text": "(most refreshingly) Mattel action figures", "signal_type": "praise", "polarity": "positive", "rubric_matches": [16, 59], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "making a genuine effort to sell their superhero properties to audiences beyond the stereotypical young boy demographic", "signal_type": "praise", "polarity": "positive", "rubric_matches": [15, 46], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "on its face is a net-positive", "signal_type": "praise", "polarity": "positive", "rubric_matches": [15, 59], "_snap_kind": "exact"}], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"passage_text": "Well, because it's not DC Comics and Warner Bros. just deciding to make an effort to make merchandise and/or toys of their existing and already popular female superheroes and supervillains. It's not just them saying \"Oh, well, this next line up will include figures and books about Harley Quinn and Batgirl, or this latest Super Friends story book will actually include Wonder Woman and/or Hawkgirl this time around.\" No, the proverbial powers-that-be, who I should stress are doing what is in the broad scheme of things a net good, are crafting a whole separate and potentially watered-down universe specifically targeting female superhero fans.", "passage_polarity": "negative", "signals": [{"signal_text": "crafting a whole separate and potentially watered-down universe specifically targeting female superhero fans", "signal_type": "complaint", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [16, 32, 59], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "not DC Comics and Warner Bros. just deciding to make an effort to make merchandise and/or toys of their existing and already popular female superheroes", "signal_type": "complaint", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [16, 59], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "potentially watered-down universe", "signal_type": "complaint", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [32, 59], "_snap_kind": "exact"}], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"passage_text": "They are basically created the LEGO Friends variation on the DC Comics super heroes. They are creating what amounts to the \"Pink Justice League.\" I'm going to try not to merely quote the entire press release, but the points that stuck out were \"Featuring DC Comics' most powerful and diverse line-up of female characters as relatable teens...\" and \"centers on the female Super Heroes and Super-Villains of the DC Comics universe during their formative years--prior to discovering their full super power potential.\" In other words, this won't be the \"real\" characters that boys and girls know and love, but rather an altered and somewhat toned-down version.", "passage_polarity": "negative", "signals": [{"signal_text": "creating what amounts to the \"Pink Justice League\"", "signal_type": "complaint", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [32, 46], "_snap_kind": "anchor_only"}, {"signal_text": "this won't be the \"real\" characters that boys and girls know and love, but rather an altered and somewhat toned-down version", "signal_type": "complaint", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [32, 59], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "prior to discovering their full super power potential", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [32, 59], "_snap_kind": "exact"}], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"passage_text": "And instead of making sets where the girls embarked on fantastical adventures, they fashioned what amounted to a Sweet Valley High melodrama. There is nothing wrong with teen girl-centric melodrama, and I don't believe that a story about a girl who does action/violence is more feminist than a story about a girl who chases romance, but the message was clear. Boys got to fight dragons, build robots, and search for treasure while the girls got to hang out at the pool and go to a juice bar .", "passage_polarity": "negative", "signals": [{"signal_text": "fashioned what amounted to a Sweet Valley High melodrama", "signal_type": "complaint", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [32, 46], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "Boys got to fight dragons, build robots, and search for treasure while the girls got to hang out at the pool and go to a juice bar", "signal_type": "complaint", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [46, 132], "_snap_kind": "exact"}], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"passage_text": "But the fact DC Comics and company couldn't just make a pledge to sell more merchandise that just happened to feature their female characters is disheartening. It would have been a lot easier to just offer McDonalds Happy Meal tie-ins with the female Young Justice characters as well as the male ones, or make DC Super Friends books that actually included female heroes in the standard line-up. It would be easier to just take their current young-skewing Super Friends and make sure it's easier to find the likes of Wonder Woman and Catwoman or Harley Quinn merchandise associated with said universe amid the Batman and Superman toys .", "passage_polarity": "negative", "signals": [{"signal_text": "couldn't just make a pledge to sell more merchandise that just happened to feature their female characters is disheartening", "signal_type": "complaint", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [16, 59], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signa