{"unit_id": "pair_1758_197356", "ok": true, "issues": [], "snap_stats": {"exact": 23, "ws_normalized": 0, "no_match": 0, "anchor_only": 0, "empty": 0}, "parsed": {"unit_id": "pair_1758_197356", "passages": [{"passage_text": "But in talks here this week, they made little headway. To take one example, when announcing the trade talks last year, leaders said that the agreement would seek to \"eliminate all tariffs\" on trade in goods between the United States and the European Union, as a step toward creating the world's biggest bilateral trade zone. But this week, American negotiators accused Europe of seeking to exclude beef, chicken and pork products from tariff cuts.", "passage_polarity": "negative", "signals": [{"signal_text": "they made little headway", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [50, 63], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "American negotiators accused Europe of seeking to exclude beef, chicken and pork products from tariff cuts", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [12, 29], "_snap_kind": "exact"}], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"passage_text": "That may prove difficult. The discussions are still at an early stage, of course. The talks this week in Brussels, led by L. Daniel Mullaney, the assistant trade representative of the United States, and by Karel De Gucht, the trade commissioner for the European Union, were only the fourth round. By contrast, talks for a grand trade pact with Asia-Pacific nations and the United States, announced in 2011, are already headed for their 22nd round.", "passage_polarity": "negative", "signals": [{"signal_text": "That may prove difficult", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [7, 30], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "only the fourth round", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "neutral", "rubric_matches": [66, 200], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "already headed for their 22nd round", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "neutral", "rubric_matches": [200, 66], "_snap_kind": "exact"}], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"passage_text": "The two negotiators largely skirted questions about thorny topics that include trade in genetically modified foods, products common in the United States market but still mostly banned in Europe. Nor did they discuss a demand by Congress that hormone-treated beef, also banned in Europe, be part of the trade talks.", "passage_polarity": "negative", "signals": [{"signal_text": "largely skirted questions about thorny topics", "signal_type": "complaint", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [13, 31], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "Nor did they discuss a demand by Congress", "signal_type": "complaint", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [13, 31], "_snap_kind": "exact"}], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"passage_text": "On the European side, civil society groups have criticized what they describe as the secrecy surrounding the talks and the apparent dominance of corporate interests in the discussions. They have been particularly incensed by a proposal for the insertion of a legal provision known as investor-state dispute settlement, which would give corporations the right to sue governments within the European Union for damages if an agreement was \"breached\" and it caused economic harm.", "passage_polarity": "negative", "signals": [{"signal_text": "criticized what they describe as the secrecy surrounding the talks", "signal_type": "complaint", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [13, 31], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "apparent dominance of corporate interests", "signal_type": "complaint", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [15, 16], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "particularly incensed by a proposal for the insertion of a legal provision known as investor-state dispute settlement", "signal_type": "complaint", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [14, 45], "_snap_kind": "exact"}], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"passage_text": "But European critics have assailed that provision as a Trojan horse for defeating their hard-won laws on consumer protection, labor and the environment, which in many cases are stronger than those in America.", "passage_polarity": "negative", "signals": [{"signal_text": "assailed that provision as a Trojan horse", "signal_type": "complaint", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [32, 26], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "defeating their hard-won laws on consumer protection, labor and the environment", "signal_type": "complaint", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [14, 15], "_snap_kind": "exact"}], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"passage_text": "The outcry led Mr. De Gucht, the European Union's trade commissioner, to announce in January that he was hitting \"the pause button\" on investor-state dispute settlement and opening a period of public consultation on the provision.", "passage_polarity": "positive", "signals": [{"signal_text": "hitting \"the pause button\" on investor-state dispute settlement", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "positive", "rubric_matches": [9, 10], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "opening a period of public consultation", "signal_type": "praise", "polarity": "positive", "rubric_matches": [18, 13], "_snap_kind": "exact"}], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"passage_text": "Stuart E. Eizenstat, a partner at the Washington law firm Covington &amp; Burling and former ambassador to the European Union, said he had been taken aback by the level of opposition to the trade talks. \"I'm more concerned than I have been since the outset of the negotiations than I would have anticipated at this point,\" Mr. Eizenstat said.", "passage_polarity": "negative", "signals": [{"signal_text": "taken aback by the level of opposition", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [47, 50], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "I'm more concerned than I have been since the outset of the negotiations", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [19, 40], "_snap_kind": "exact"}], "_snap_kind": "exact"}]}, "raw_text": "{\"unit_id\": \"pair_1758_197356\", \"passages\": [{\"passage_text\": \"But in talks here this week, they made little headway. To take one example, when announcing the trade talks last year, leaders said that the agreement would seek to \\\"eliminate all tariffs\\\" on trade in goods between the United States and the European Union, as a step toward creating the world's biggest bilateral trade zone. But this week, American negotiators accused Europe of seeking to exclude beef, chicken and pork products from tariff cuts.\", \"passage_polarity\": \"negative\", \"signals\": [{\"signal_text\": \"they made little headway\", \"signal_type\": \"observation\", \"polarity\": \"negative\", \"rubric_matches\": [50, 63]}, {\"signal_text\": \"American negotiators accused Europe of seeking to exclude beef, chicken and pork products from tariff cuts\", \"signal_type\": \"observation\", \"polarity\": \"negative\", \"rubric_matches\": [12, 29]}]}, {\"passage_text\": \"That may prove difficult. The discussions are still at an early stage, of course. The talks this week in Brussels, led by L. Daniel Mullaney, the assistant trade representative of the United States, and by Karel De Gucht, the trade commissioner for the European Union, were only the fourth round. By contrast, talks for a grand trade pact with Asia-Pacific nations and the United States, announced in 2011, are already headed for their 22nd round.\", \"passage_polarity\": \"negative\", \"signals\": [{\"signal_text\": \"That may prove difficult\", \"signal_type\": \"observation\", \"polarity\": \"negative\", \"rubric_matches\": [7, 30]}, {\"signal_text\": \"only the fourth round\", \"signal_type\": \"observation\", \"polarity\": \"neutral\", \"rubric_matches\": [66, 200]}, {\"signal_text\": \"already headed for their 22nd round\", \"signal_type\": \"obser