gration and Customs Enforcement (\"ICE\") grant Scott-Jones deferred action status", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [31, 8], "_snap_kind": "exact"}], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"passage_text": "On January 3, 2013, Scott-Jones was sentenced to 18 months in federal prison, and just like Joe, was not eligible for a prison camp, despite the verbal promises given to him by government prosecutors. He reported to prison and served the majority of his sentence in Folkston, GA, a facility run by private prison company GEO . The D. Ray James Detention Center houses male inmates who are non-U.S. citizens in a secure, razor-wire fenced prison.", "passage_polarity": "negative", "signals": [{"signal_text": "despite the verbal promises given to him by government prosecutors", "signal_type": "complaint", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [31, 12], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "was not eligible for a prison camp", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [30, 8], "_snap_kind": "exact"}], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"passage_text": "It turns out, halfway houses are also a privilege just for American citizens. So, upon completion of his prison sentence on May 23, 2014, Scott-Jones was surprised when instead of being picked up by his wife, he was immediately detained and escorted by ICE agents to an immigration detention facility, where he would be held pending deportation to the U.K.", "passage_polarity": "negative", "signals": [{"signal_text": "halfway houses are also a privilege just for American citizens", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [30, 8], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "he was immediately detained and escorted by ICE agents to an immigration detention facility, where he would be held pending deportation to the U.K.", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [31, 8], "_snap_kind": "exact"}], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"passage_text": "It was a shock considering that Scott-Jones believed his plea and cooperation with government prosecutors would protect him from this very scenario. ICE transferred Scott-Jones to a county jail in Ocilla, GA, a remote town in the southern part of the state, and later to Stewart Detention Facility in Lumpkin, GA.", "passage_polarity": "negative", "signals": [{"signal_text": "Scott-Jones believed his plea and cooperation with government prosecutors would protect him from this very scenario", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [31, 8], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "It was a shock", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [31, 8], "_snap_kind": "exact"}], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"passage_text": "In an interview she told me that it is not uncommon for individuals, such as Scott-Jones, who have lived in the U.S for many years and have established strong familial, professional and economic ties to this country, to face deportation. Many of them never give a second thought to the possibility of being deported. \"The term 'Lawful Permanent Resident' doesn't actually confer permanent status, as one might assume,\" Ms. Sohahong explained.", "passage_polarity": "negative", "signals": [{"signal_text": "it is not uncommon for individuals... to face deportation", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [66, 50], "_snap_kind": "anchor_only"}, {"signal_text": "\"The term 'Lawful Permanent Resident' doesn't actually confer permanent status, as one might assume,\"", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [30, 8], "_snap_kind": "exact"}], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"passage_text": "This was exactly the predicament Scott-Jones found himself in. Despite having lawfully lived and worked in the U.S. for over 30 years, being married to a U.S. citizen for nearly 20 years, and having children and step-children in this country, ICE was seeking to deport him to the U.K., where he no longer had any ties.", "passage_polarity": "negative", "signals": [{"signal_text": "Despite having lawfully lived and worked in the U.S. for over 30 years... ICE was seeking to deport him to the U.K., where he no longer had any ties", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [66, 50], "_snap_kind": "anchor_only"}], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"passage_text": "Initially, Ms. Sohahong did not think there was much that could be done to stave off Scott-Jones' deportation and keep him in the country. \"Given the severity of Mr. Scott-Jones' crimes, he was classified as an 'aggravated felon' in the immigration context,\" Ms. Sohahong said. This essentially means that he had no defense against being deported, unless he could show a strong likelihood that he would face torture in the country to which ICE was seeking to deport him, in this case the U.K. That would be impossible.", "passage_polarity": "negative", "signals": [{"signal_text": "he was classified as an 'aggravated felon' in the immigration context", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [30, 8], "_snap_kind": "exact"}, {"signal_text": "he had no defense against being deported", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [30, 8], "_snap_kind": "exact"}], "_snap_kind": "exact"}]}, "raw_text": "{\"unit_id\": \"pair_19703_51623\", \"passages\": [{\"passage_text\": \"Now that Teresa has completed her sentence and returned home, Joe is set to start his prison term in March. Joe's prison stay is going to be different, because unlike Teresa, he is not a U.S. citizen. He is an Italian citizen who has a status as a \\\"Lawful Permanent Resident of the U.S.\\\" who has lived in the country since he was a toddler.\", \"passage_polarity\": \"neutral\", \"signals\": [{\"signal_text\": \"Joe's prison stay is going to be different, because unlike Teresa, he is not a U.S. citizen\", \"sig